# Feature Gaps Between `TODO_ITEMS/AUDIT.md` And Current Product Surface

Last reviewed: Wednesday, August 12, 2026

## What This File Is

This file captures the gap between:

- the broad audit matrix in [`TODO_ITEMS/AUDIT.md`](/C:/Users/Abi/Desktop/github/runledger-community/TODO_ITEMS/AUDIT.md)
- the actual UI and backend feature surface currently exposed by the web app and API routers
- the detailed route inventory generated in [`C:\Users\Abi\Desktop\runledger-feature-list.md`](</C:/Users/Abi/Desktop/runledger-feature-list.md>)

The goal is to make audit work executable against the real product, not only against planned platform capabilities.

## High-Level Findings

- `AUDIT.md` is a good domain-level matrix, but it is not aligned tightly enough to the actual dashboard route structure.
- The current product exposes many concrete UI pages that are not represented as distinct audit targets in `AUDIT.md`.
- `AUDIT.md` also includes several infrastructure, SDK, and external-stack features that are not visible in the current sidebar-driven UI and should be audited separately from product-page audits.
- Some current UI pages reflect legacy concepts (`Projects`, `Team Models`, `Teams / Workspaces`) that the repo guidance says should not be expanded.
- Some major UI areas bundle multiple subfeatures into one row in `AUDIT.md`, which will make real audits too coarse to be useful.

## Gap Type 1: UI/Backend Features Present In Product But Missing As Distinct Audit Items

These are real pages or routed surfaces in the dashboard that should exist as first-class audit targets.

### Observe

- `Request Flow Focus` at `/request-flow/focus`
- `Runs detail` at `/runs/{run_id}` should be separate from list-level `Runs`
- `Sessions detail` at `/sessions/{session_id}` should be separate from list-level `Sessions`
- `Analytics user detail` at `/analytics/users/{end_user_id}`
- `Billing summary` at `/billing-summary`
- `Global dashboard` at `/global-dashboard`
- `Organization dashboard` at `/organization/dashboard`

